re with the original persona 5 it's a  lot more black and white and good versus  evil  and the third semester is really really  great but beyond that there's so much  content in this 125 hour jrpg  and more specifically so much new  content in this 125 hour jrpg  that it's so hard to talk about  everything that's great with persona 5  royal in just one minute  so because of this news third semester  as well as the new characters the new  music the new area  those are the reasons that it makes  persona 5 royal a whole new experience  from the original persona 5 and it's why  it's one of gamespot's top 10 games of  2020.  shall we  [Music]  checkmate  y'all gotta look at the bigger picture  here nothing worth fighting for was ever  won without sacrifice  your fears your worries  your concerns take fifa and get out of  here  whatever your problem  i got you there are a whole lot of  reasons why i think final fantasy 7  remake  is one of the best games of 2020 but for  me the thing that really  makes it stick with me is that it  reminded me why  final fantasy vii is so iconic and why  people  herald it as the best game of all time  over time  i forgot what it is that final fantasy  really does well because  final fantasy kind of forgot it for a  while but with final fantasy 7 remake  realized what its strengths were again  and that is this idea of you as a player  going on a massive adventure with a  bunch of characters that you  start off not really knowing build an  intimate friendship with  to the point where when you finish the  game you feel like you're saying goodbye  to friends and it  really hurts and you long to be with  them again  and that's the core of final fantasy  that's what makes a great final fantasy  game  it reminded me why i love final fantasy  as a franchise and that's why i think  final fantasy 7  remake is one of the best games of 2020.  [Music]  our beloved planet is dying slowly  silently can you bear to see the planet  suffer  cloud  we're gonna make it home all of us  no exceptions  [Music]  please get up  what stands out the most about the last  of us part two is the incredible lanes  that naughty dog went  to dial up the stakes of the game the  action is thrilling  the stealth in the game is tense and the  set pieces had me at the edge of my seat  the gameplay is some of the most  immersive that i've seen and there was  never a dull moment with every encounter  whether it was from human enemy factions  or just  hordes of clickers chock full of  heart-pounding moments  the story has all the bones of a classic  western revenge tale with some twists  and turns  but it's these certain moments in the  game that kind of stand out almost like  their own vignettes  that are just some of the most beautiful  moments every dark pit in the story that  the game asks you to traverse  will be met with these beautiful pock  marks of light that just steep through  the cracks  and will stay with you for hours on end  and the perfect balance of bittersweet  in this game is just  masterfully crafted if there's one good  thing about this year  is that i had the pleasure of playing  the last of us part two and it's for all  of these reasons and more  this game is one of gamespot's best  games of 2020.  i don't know what happened she needed  her immunity  to mean something  maybe i just want to do right by her  [Music]  i swore to protect this island with my  life  but now the mongols have stolen our home  killed or some right  [Music]  he forgot what it's like to fight  someone stronger than you  go satsushima came in a year that open  world games seem to be coming by the  dozens but  what made tsushima unique was its  respect for the natural world and the  player's place within it  jin sakai is a samurai who struggles  with inner conflict between upholding  the tradition and protecting the people  and this element translates to the world  in a powerful and meaningful way  both through its story and through its  combat flu